NPM lru-cache regression in Bun v0.5.7 due to timeout.unref()

* Page: GitHub issue
* URL: https://github.com/oven-sh/bun/issues/2466
* State: closed (completed)
* Author: spiffytech
* Created: 2023-03-23T14:18:43Z
* Updated: 2024-02-04T08:56:56Z
* Repository: oven-sh/bun
* Number: #2466
* Comments: 3

Labels

* bug
* node.js

What version of Bun is running?

0.5.8

What platform is your computer?

Linux (Fedora 37, kernel 6.1.18-200)

What steps can reproduce the bug?

Beginning in Bun v0.5.7, the lru-cache NPM module no longer expires entries that exceed the cache TTL.
(TTL is  in milliseconds). The delayed tryGet() which should clearly be expired and print Miss, instead prints Hit.
In Bun v0.4.0, the delayed tryGet() correctly prints Miss.
import LRU from "lru-cache";

const lru = new LRU({
  max: 3,
  ttl: 3,
});

const tryGet = () => {
  const value = lru.get("foo");
  if (value) {
    console.log("Hit");
  } else {
    console.log("Miss");
  }
};

lru.set("foo", "bar");
tryGet();
tryGet();

await new Promise((resolve) => setTimeout(resolve, 500));
tryGet();

What is the expected behavior?

Cache items should Miss when expired.

What do you see instead?

Cache items continue to Hit indefinitely.

Additional information

lru-cache will unref a timeout when possible. If I delete the lines for the unref call, correct behavior is restored.
This suggests Bun's implementation of timeout.unref() (IIRC introduced in v0.5.7) is malfunctioning.
(The repro code works fine in Node.js, too).

